<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="042" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Regarding-vs-related intent — classify `file-to-existing | update-existing | new-record-related-to`; demote the identifier on "new filing based on X" (suppress auto-file); propose gated `dataverse.create_record` linking the referenced record as related</title>
    <phase>P4 — Job C + intent</phase>
    <gate>after:020,022</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>bff-api, catalog, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Intent classification that GATES auto-file behavior on the association path — a misclassification silently misfiles email onto the wrong record (misfiling = #1 trust-killer). Introduces the "related-to" relationship distinctly from "regarding" (ADR-024 path-A exception) WITHOUT a second regarding mechanism. Touches the shared association/auto-file path + the gated create path. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The intent boundary (regarding vs related; "new filing based on X" demotes rather than files) is subtle and safety-critical — the exact reasoning that, done sloppily, misfiles email; and representing "related-to" without a second regarding mechanism (ADR-024 path-A) needs careful judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches the shared association / auto-file path + `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` + the gated create path; serialize among shared `Services/Communication/` writers. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>020, 022</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement **regarding-vs-related intent** (FR-12): classify each email's intent as `file-to-existing | update-existing | new-record-related-to`. When phrasing like **"new filing based on X"** appears, **demote** the identifier X from *regarding* to *related* and **suppress auto-file** onto X. On `new-record-related-to`, propose creating a NEW record (gated `dataverse.create_record`) that **links the referenced record X as related** — NOT filed onto X.

    Represent the "related-to" relationship **distinctly from "regarding"** WITHOUT introducing a second regarding mechanism — this is an **ADR-024 path-A exception** (document the relationship model). Reuse the one regarding mechanism (resolver-only write) for actual regarding; represent "related-to" as a separate, documented relationship.

    Reach AI **only** through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (ADR-013 facade) as a **code-directed Action + Binding** (ADR-039). MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine. Reuse the gated `dataverse.create_record` tool for the create (as Job C does) — do NOT fork a second create mechanism. The create is **proposed** (offered as create-new / file-onto / link-related), gated + human-confirmed; nothing auto-finalizes on the `new-record-related-to` branch (NFR-06 / ADR-015). **NFR-04:** best-effort / non-fatal.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication + Ai domains, authoritative on the association / auto-file path (020/021), ADR-024 (one regarding mechanism; resolver-only write; the path-A exception for representing "related-to" distinctly), ADR-039 (code-directed Action + Binding), ADR-013 (PublicContracts facade), the gated `dataverse.create_record` tool, and NFR-06 / ADR-015 (proposed + confirmed, nothing auto-finalizes on the create branch).
  </role>

  <goal>
    An email's intent is classified `file-to-existing | update-existing | new-record-related-to`. "New filing based on X" demotes X from regarding to related and suppresses auto-file onto X; the system offers create-new / file-onto / link-related rather than silently filing onto X. On `new-record-related-to`, a gated `dataverse.create_record` is proposed that links X as related (via a documented "related-to" relationship distinct from "regarding", no second regarding mechanism — ADR-024 path-A). AI reached only via `PublicContracts`; the create reuses the gated create tool; nothing auto-finalizes on the create branch. Best-effort on the enrichment path. Build clean; unit + seam tests + a golden-utterance eval case pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported; the relationship model documented.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The single biggest misfiling risk: an email that references record X but is actually about a NEW related matter ("new filing based on PAT-908068") must NOT auto-file onto X. FR-12 detects that intent and demotes the identifier from regarding to related, then offers create-new / file-onto / link-related. This is the intent layer above the deterministic identifier rung (020) + the C-1 auto-file narrowing (021) — it can SUPPRESS an auto-file the rung would otherwise do.

      ADR-024 owns the one polymorphic regarding mechanism (resolver-only write). "Related-to" is a genuinely different relationship — but building a SECOND regarding mechanism is forbidden. The resolution (spec §6.5 / ADR Tensions) is path-A: represent "related-to" distinctly (a documented relationship) while leaving "regarding" to the one resolver mechanism. Document the relationship model.

      The create on the `new-record-related-to` branch reuses the gated `dataverse.create_record` tool (as Job C / 040 does) — proposed + confirmed, never auto-finalized (NFR-06 / ADR-015).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AutoFileGate.cs (REFERENCE — the auto-file gate this intent can SUPPRESS on "new filing based on X")</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs (REFERENCE — association status; demoted identifier → related, not regarding auto-file)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs (REFERENCE — the classification substrate; intent reuses the signal, no 2nd full LLM pass)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (REUSE — facade seam; intent Action + the gated create go through here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs (REFERENCE — the one regarding mechanism; "related-to" is represented distinctly, NOT via a second map)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md (one regarding mechanism; resolver-only write; path-A exception for "related-to")</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/inputschemas/create-task-v1.input.schema.json (REFERENCE — the gated-create pattern shape reused for the related-record create)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/tasks/040-job-c-email-triggered-work-create-task.poml (the gated-create precedent to mirror)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>020 (the identifier association this intent can demote), 022 (the classification signal reused for intent).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-12">Scope: classify intent `file-to-existing | update-existing | new-record-related-to`; "new filing based on X" DEMOTES the identifier from regarding to related + SUPPRESSES auto-file onto X; on `new-record-related-to`, propose a gated `dataverse.create_record` linking X as related. Offer create-new / file-onto / link-related — never silently file onto X.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024 (path-A exception)">Scope: represent "related-to" DISTINCTLY from "regarding" WITHOUT a second regarding mechanism; reuse the one resolver-only regarding mechanism for actual regarding; document the "related-to" relationship model. This is a documented path-A exception (spec §6.5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: code-directed Action + Binding via catalog data; MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine; reuse the gated `dataverse.create_record` tool (no forked create).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-03">Scope: reach AI ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` into Communication code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-015">Scope: the create on `new-record-related-to` is proposed + human-confirmed (gated); nothing auto-finalizes on this branch; privilege flagged never decided.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C-1 / FR-03">Scope: this intent interacts with the C-1 auto-file narrowing (021) — it can only SUPPRESS an auto-file, never widen it; a demoted identifier does not auto-file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04 / ADR-045">Scope: intent classification is best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send / enrichment path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (extends the association/auto-file path + reuses the gated create via PublicContracts; catalog data, no new service, no second regarding mechanism); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests + seam tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07 / ADR-039">Scope: the intent Action/Binding adds a golden-utterance eval case (blocking merge gate) — incl. the "new filing based on X" demotion case.</constraint>
  </constraints>

