  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, ADR-024 (one regarding mechanism + the path-A exception rationale), ADR-039, ADR-013, ADR-015, the spec §6.5 ADR Tensions (ADR-024 path-A), and 040's gated-create decisions.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `AutoFileGate.cs`, `AssociationStatusMapper.cs`, `RegardingFieldMap.cs`, and `AiClassificationRung.cs` — identify where auto-file happens (so intent can suppress it), how the one regarding mechanism writes, and where the classification signal is available.</step>
    <step order="3">Author the intent Action + Binding (catalog data) reusing the classification signal (022) that classifies `file-to-existing | update-existing | new-record-related-to`; grep to confirm there is no existing intent layer (§11 evidence).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the demotion: on `new-record-related-to` ("new filing based on X"), demote X from regarding to related + SUPPRESS the auto-file onto X (via `AutoFileGate` / `AssociationStatusMapper`); surface create-new / file-onto / link-related as options — never silently file onto X.</step>
    <step order="5">Design + document the "related-to" relationship distinctly from "regarding" (ADR-024 path-A) — NO second regarding mechanism; the one resolver mechanism still owns "regarding". Document the relationship model in the PR / a design note.</step>
    <step order="6">On `new-record-related-to`, propose a gated `dataverse.create_record` (reuse the gated-create pattern from 040) that links X as related; proposed + human-confirmed, nothing auto-finalizes (NFR-06 / ADR-015). Wire best-effort onto the enrichment path (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="7">Add the golden-utterance eval case (NFR-07) incl. the "new filing based on X" demotion. Write unit + seam tests: (a) "new filing based on PAT-908068" does NOT auto-file onto PAT-908068; it offers create-new / file-onto / link-related; (b) `file-to-existing` still auto-files per C-1 (intent only suppresses, never widens); (c) the create links X as related via the documented relationship — NO second regarding mechanism (grep-verifiable); (d) the create is proposed + confirmed, never auto-finalized; (e) intent failure does not fail the enrichment path (NFR-04). ADR-038 boundary mocks only.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus no-misfile on demotion, no second regarding mechanism, reuse gated create, facade discipline, non-fatal); `adr-check` against ADR-024 (path-A) / ADR-039 / ADR-013 / ADR-015 + spec FR-12 / C-1 / NFR-04 / NFR-06 / NFR-07. Address Critical findings; cite the path-A exception + Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` association path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (042 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (intent taxonomy, demotion wiring point, the documented related-to relationship model, gated-create reuse).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If representing "related-to" distinctly cannot be done without either (a) a second regarding mechanism (ADR-024 violation) or (b) an ambiguous intent boundary where "new filing based on X" cannot be reliably separated from "file onto X" — STOP and surface per root §6 / §6.5 (this is the ADR-024 path-A exception; confirm the resolution or escalate). Do NOT add a second regarding mechanism and do NOT ship an intent classifier that silently misfiles on the ambiguous boundary.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The identifier rung (020) + C-1 auto-file gate (021) associate + auto-file; the one ADR-024 regarding mechanism writes regarding; the gated `dataverse.create_record` (040) creates records. There is no intent layer that distinguishes "about X" from "new thing related to X".</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a new intent Action + Binding (catalog data) that reuses the classification signal + the auto-file gate + the gated create; "related-to" is represented as a documented distinct relationship (ADR-024 path-A), NOT a second regarding mechanism; no new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without intent, "new filing based on PAT-908068" silently auto-files onto PAT-908068 (misfiling = #1 trust-killer) and there is no way to link a genuinely new related record — FR-12 / Success Criterion 3 fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect the auto-file gate, status mapper, regarding map, classification substrate, facade, ADR-024</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm no existing intent layer (§11); confirm NO second regarding mechanism introduced; confirm gated-create reuse</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Author the intent Action/Binding + demotion wiring + related-to relationship + gated-create proposal</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, unit/seam tests, eval-case render, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
