    <criterion testable="true">`file-to-existing` intent still auto-files per C-1 (021) — the intent layer only SUPPRESSES auto-file, never widens it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On `new-record-related-to`, a gated `dataverse.create_record` is proposed that links the referenced record as related via a documented "related-to" relationship — NO second regarding mechanism is introduced (ADR-024 path-A; grep-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The related-record create is proposed + human-confirmed; nothing auto-finalizes on the `new-record-related-to` branch (NFR-06 / ADR-015).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AI reached only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; the create reuses the gated `dataverse.create_record` (no forked create); no capability landed on the frozen node engine.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Intent classification is best-effort: a failure does NOT fail the capture or send / enrichment path (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A golden-utterance eval case (incl. the "new filing based on X" demotion) exists and passes (NFR-07); `dotnet build` clean; tests pass; publish-size delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    The safety-critical property is: never silently misfile on "new filing based on X". "Related-to" is represented distinctly from "regarding" without a second regarding mechanism (ADR-024 path-A exception — document it in the PR). Reuse the gated create (040) — do not fork. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` association path).
  </notes>

